sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/aristotle-ga04-10> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "When the movement from the father in the semen is weakened ('resolved'), it changes into that of his father and then his grandfather, and likewise in the maternal line, so that children may resemble grandparents and remoter ancestors.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Unmastered paternal movements revert to those of the grandfather";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Aristotle, On the Generation of Animals (De Generatione Animalium), Book IV; translated by Arthur Platt, The Works of Aristotle Translated into English, ed. J. A. Smith and W. D. Ross, Oxford: Clarendon Press, vol. V (1912). Scope: humans and animals generally"
}
